<Chapter xmlns:aid="http://ns.adobe.com/AdobeInDesign/4.0/" id="original-interior-proof"><Content aid:pstyle="ChapterHeader">A byte becomes a running world&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">Design proof using retained teaching passages from the current manuscripts. Source selections and asset hashes are recorded beside this file. This sample is not a final book.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">The volume begins with a saved material appearing correctly after an editor is reopened, then traces the agreements that make that possible: interpretation, representation, storage, identity, and ownership. This chapter establishes the byte-level vocabulary and numeric contracts that later chapters rely on.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">Imagine a small editor with a metal panel in its viewport. You change the panel’s material, save the scene, close the editor, and reopen it. The surface looks the same. That simple result depends on several different agreements.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">The scene file must encode a stable material reference. The importer must recognize the referenced source asset and produce a usable runtime artifact. The executable must contain compatible code for reading that artifact. A resource manager must keep the uploaded texture alive while the renderer uses it. The panel’s entity identifier must continue to name the intended entity even if component storage moves.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">Inline notation belongs to the sentence&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">For unsigned value <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/7747049d8d5e59802a50d60a59f18c55573d8a02593b56e0d3d88d321d1279a9.pdf" alt="x" jobId="0cfb135b111632e99e113052" originalTeX="x" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/0cfb135b111632e99e113052.svg" sourceWidthPt="7.117" sourceHeightPt="5.637" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-0.1375" /> stored in <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/be99a5d39428ad74b56efa4420ad6b8187b61b24a2ada25462e8d38467062bcc.pdf" alt="n" jobId="7e0169371fd671a4ffc5c604" originalTeX="n" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/7e0169371fd671a4ffc5c604.svg" sourceWidthPt="7.463" sourceHeightPt="5.637" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-0.1375" /> octets, with byte index <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/37cefa148a8e3b7d9d19f9aed85681f4907b361c8af330843447c170fefcb816.pdf" alt="i" jobId="c9a9aab9bd49b5120a91abe6" originalTeX="i" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/c9a9aab9bd49b5120a91abe6.svg" sourceWidthPt="4.296" sourceHeightPt="8.36" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-0.1375" /> starting at zero:&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">For little endian, add each byte with its weight: <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/3d2b10f1a72cd40ce9f9ccc1e9e24b5200d7aa77d32adc1cc96a9e671c0a9d49.pdf" alt="120+86\times256+52\times256^2+18\times256^3" jobId="fa3e4e5724b7066fe8a1433f" originalTeX="120+86\times256+52\times256^2+18\times256^3" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/fa3e4e5724b7066fe8a1433f.svg" sourceWidthPt="214.126007" sourceHeightPt="11.77" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-1.023" /> gives the same answer.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content"><Link href="#appendix-a1f7c53b4742">Alignment</Link> <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/37394276a38c9b15e22adc034d20c49d9a45af95a53ab9648e6d10669c4a0dd4.pdf" alt="A" jobId="6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715" originalTeX="A" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715.svg" sourceWidthPt="9.334" sourceHeightPt="8.91" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="0" /> means an object’s start must lie at an address divisible by <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/37394276a38c9b15e22adc034d20c49d9a45af95a53ab9648e6d10669c4a0dd4.pdf" alt="A" jobId="6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715" originalTeX="A" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715.svg" sourceWidthPt="9.334" sourceHeightPt="8.91" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="0" />. <Strong aid:cstyle="Bold">Padding</Strong> is space inserted to satisfy placement or stride requirements; it is not an additional data member. In C++, <InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">alignof(T)</InlineCode> reports the type’s alignment and <InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">sizeof(T)</InlineCode> its complete-object size in C++ bytes. <InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">alignas</InlineCode> can request a supported stronger alignment. An <Link href="#appendix-c4ac6bb0fff8">ABI</Link>, or application binary interface, specifies concrete conventions used when compiled components interact, including layout and calling conventions.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">For numeric byte offset <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/6ebd7aae676f0d98b31e7e32d980d358b490722326dd5507bd6d6b2f245adc0a.pdf" alt="p" jobId="df25e600d976a703c705ec86" originalTeX="p" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/df25e600d976a703c705ec86.svg" sourceWidthPt="6.259" sourceHeightPt="7.915" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-2.4145" /> and positive alignment <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/37394276a38c9b15e22adc034d20c49d9a45af95a53ab9648e6d10669c4a0dd4.pdf" alt="A" jobId="6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715" originalTeX="A" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715.svg" sourceWidthPt="9.334" sourceHeightPt="8.91" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="0" />, upward rounding is:&#13;</Content><Formula aid:pstyle="Formula" display="block"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/763d7a6f70e03c02a433ba9b05af434582a6afb817640f002e0f2e29586b4b4b.pdf" alt="&#10;\operatorname{alignUp}(p,A)=A\left\lceil p/A\right\rceil&#10;" jobId="28d31a9826e59de22566a7db" originalTeX="&#10;\operatorname{alignUp}(p,A)=A\left\lceil p/A\right\rceil&#10;" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/28d31a9826e59de22566a7db.svg" sourceWidthPt="134.199997" sourceHeightPt="12.441" baseFontPt="11.0" />&#13;</Formula><Content aid:pstyle="Content">The ceiling <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/781bee04ff6a81f92f02a2e980d0e8fc2d4fd3d29e5542ae7208884d6d0fba2b.pdf" alt="\lceil q\rceil" jobId="e493c543dd67ad9d2e9ef4ee" originalTeX="\lceil q\rceil" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/e493c543dd67ad9d2e9ef4ee.svg" sourceWidthPt="16.775" sourceHeightPt="12.441" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-3.1129999999999995" /> is the smallest integer not less than <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/61d5cbca9fb1b1aeeece3eefce598c687b67e4a8ba9f8af89733f1883d79f528.pdf" alt="q" jobId="8de0ad9ec33a4617bea95024" originalTeX="q" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/8de0ad9ec33a4617bea95024.svg" sourceWidthPt="5.725" sourceHeightPt="7.915" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-2.4145" />. For <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/6c90eb8139f0bfa01fdd44cfc7f4a8b444259430a96831f7d9ab21c939cdfa6a.pdf" alt="p=13,A=8" jobId="94bc349c2b0dd443a685db00" originalTeX="p=13,A=8" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/94bc349c2b0dd443a685db00.svg" sourceWidthPt="72.980003" sourceHeightPt="11.325" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-2.4145" />, the next multiple is 16, so three bytes are skipped. If <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/6ebd7aae676f0d98b31e7e32d980d358b490722326dd5507bd6d6b2f245adc0a.pdf" alt="p" jobId="df25e600d976a703c705ec86" originalTeX="p" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/df25e600d976a703c705ec86.svg" sourceWidthPt="6.259" sourceHeightPt="7.915" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-2.4145" /> is already 16, it stays 16. A safe implementation can compute the remainder, determine the needed increment, then check that the increment fits before adding. For power-of-two <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/37394276a38c9b15e22adc034d20c49d9a45af95a53ab9648e6d10669c4a0dd4.pdf" alt="A" jobId="6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715" originalTeX="A" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715.svg" sourceWidthPt="9.334" sourceHeightPt="8.91" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="0" />, <InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">(p &amp; (A-1)) == 0</InlineCode> tests alignment; the common <InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">(p+A-1)&amp;~(A-1)</InlineCode> shortcut still needs an overflow check and the power-of-two precondition.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">A display equation needs its own space&#13;</Content><Formula aid:pstyle="Formula" display="block"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/ccd386263fc4147f093210b813be6c7a8cf4e390eaba188025681128c1c815b5.pdf" alt="&#10;b_i^{\mathrm{LE}}=\left\lfloor x/256^i\right\rfloor\bmod256,\qquad&#10;b_i^{\mathrm{BE}}=\left\lfloor x/256^{n-1-i}\right\rfloor\bmod256&#10;" jobId="4bc52ac02bda8ecd57b31625" originalTeX="&#10;b_i^{\mathrm{LE}}=\left\lfloor x/256^i\right\rfloor\bmod256,\qquad&#10;b_i^{\mathrm{BE}}=\left\lfloor x/256^{n-1-i}\right\rfloor\bmod256&#10;" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/4bc52ac02bda8ecd57b31625.svg" sourceWidthPt="317.23999" sourceHeightPt="15.499" baseFontPt="11.0" />&#13;</Formula><Content aid:pstyle="Content">The next paragraph must begin below the equation, with its spaces and baseline intact. The expression above is retained from the byte-order lesson.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">Build a matrix from its measured basis images&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">So knowing the two basis images determines the output of every vector. Suppose the calibration sends&#13;</Content><Formula aid:pstyle="Formula" display="block"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/90429ea9e8f686bbc0c9ce581d8c1fe4fbee2136fbaca53541b33e22a5c415d5.pdf" alt="&#10;T(\mathbf e_1)=\begin{bmatrix}2\\1\end{bmatrix},\qquad&#10;T(\mathbf e_2)=\begin{bmatrix}-1\\3\end{bmatrix}.&#10;" jobId="8b46f6ade6fb8f8cc7e05a1a" originalTeX="&#10;T(\mathbf e_1)=\begin{bmatrix}2\\1\end{bmatrix},\qquad&#10;T(\mathbf e_2)=\begin{bmatrix}-1\\3\end{bmatrix}.&#10;" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/8b46f6ade6fb8f8cc7e05a1a.svg" sourceWidthPt="176.335007" sourceHeightPt="29.865" baseFontPt="11.0" />&#13;</Formula><Content aid:pstyle="Content">Put those images into the columns:&#13;</Content><Formula aid:pstyle="Formula" display="block"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/ff62a758d5698c655fc1fccf94854d1744f462635e0fc4fdb132153ff90e8457.pdf" alt="&#10;A=\begin{bmatrix}2&amp;-1\\1&amp;3\end{bmatrix}.&#10;" jobId="9481701aaf91c63f2cd2271c" originalTeX="&#10;A=\begin{bmatrix}2&amp;-1\\1&amp;3\end{bmatrix}.&#10;" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/9481701aaf91c63f2cd2271c.svg" sourceWidthPt="77.093002" sourceHeightPt="29.865" baseFontPt="11.0" />&#13;</Formula><Content aid:pstyle="Content">The columns tell us where the input basis directions go. For <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/085e03321fc281a9ae817a860b3879d7b29ec5f0ee16e4848036dbf7c9147b3e.pdf" alt="\mathbf x=(4,2)^{\mathsf T}" jobId="58b29628b482b3fa71239f67" originalTeX="\mathbf x=(4,2)^{\mathsf T}" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/58b29628b482b3fa71239f67.svg" sourceWidthPt="58.827999" sourceHeightPt="13.684" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-3.1129999999999995" />, retain the same input coefficients but combine the new directions:&#13;</Content><Formula aid:pstyle="Formula" display="block"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/3da5dd41c3547954aca1888eba60c956d01df9b756e64097a407651800acfb94.pdf" alt="&#10;A\mathbf x&#10;=4\begin{bmatrix}2\\1\end{bmatrix}&#10;+2\begin{bmatrix}-1\\3\end{bmatrix}&#10;=\begin{bmatrix}8\\4\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}-2\\6\end{bmatrix}&#10;=\begin{bmatrix}6\\10\end{bmatrix}.&#10;" jobId="7cd1165245f740e59675eeaf" originalTeX="&#10;A\mathbf x&#10;=4\begin{bmatrix}2\\1\end{bmatrix}&#10;+2\begin{bmatrix}-1\\3\end{bmatrix}&#10;=\begin{bmatrix}8\\4\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}-2\\6\end{bmatrix}&#10;=\begin{bmatrix}6\\10\end{bmatrix}.&#10;" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/7cd1165245f740e59675eeaf.svg" sourceWidthPt="239.535995" sourceHeightPt="29.865" baseFontPt="11.0" />&#13;</Formula><Content aid:pstyle="Content">This is matrix-vector multiplication. The arithmetic comes directly from preserving the vector’s basis expansion. In general, if <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/b828871c60b3c7e7ae2e1fb72a17f1bf614df3fcb2134a9b83c6c406f9cae942.pdf" alt="\mathbf c_j" jobId="01c72ad8b2dceec13a5c2994" originalTeX="\mathbf c_j" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/01c72ad8b2dceec13a5c2994.svg" sourceWidthPt="11.017" sourceHeightPt="9.3" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-3.6630000000000003" /> is column <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/e67d77bc3abf6a7a2a1287b307ecf2d351a03ce30d6f3edda1a75cff4f89aca2.pdf" alt="j" jobId="ce2f1083717013be91c13bbf" originalTeX="j" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/ce2f1083717013be91c13bbf.svg" sourceWidthPt="5.126" sourceHeightPt="10.764" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="-2.541" /> of <Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/37394276a38c9b15e22adc034d20c49d9a45af95a53ab9648e6d10669c4a0dd4.pdf" alt="A" jobId="6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715" originalTeX="A" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/math/6372fce2b4dc5c2cf6a13715.svg" sourceWidthPt="9.334" sourceHeightPt="8.91" baseFontPt="11.0" baselineShiftPt="0" />,&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">Keep comparisons in their columns&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content"><Table aid:table="table" aid:trows="5" aid:tcols="3" sourceHeadRows="1"><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="91.97200980955661"><Content aid:pstyle="Caption">Address&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="154.1139950952217"><Content aid:pstyle="Caption"><Link href="#appendix-367b6abf460e">Little-endian</Link> byte&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="149.9139950952217"><Content aid:pstyle="Caption"><Link href="#appendix-92e040df969a">Big-endian</Link> byte&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="91.97200980955661"><Content aid:pstyle="TableCell"><InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">0x1000</InlineCode>&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="154.1139950952217"><Content aid:pstyle="TableCell"><InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">78</InlineCode> — lowest significance&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="149.9139950952217"><Content aid:pstyle="TableCell"><InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">12</InlineCode> — highest significance&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="91.97200980955661"><Content aid:pstyle="TableCell"><InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">0x1001</InlineCode>&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="154.1139950952217"><Content aid:pstyle="TableCell"><InlineCode aid:cstyle="InlineCode">56</InlineCode>&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwi