</Code>&#13;<Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">Choose the direction that explains the process&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Figure"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/8f9203e5d8dfb03b340276daee604678a1f4e0c8eb9475de490e253b8c6699b0.pdf" alt="Diagram" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/mermaid/d21d21b04281361cfda13e69.svg" sourceWidthPt="199.898438" sourceHeightPt="507.449982" baseFontPt="12.0" />&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Caption">One stored value travels through interpretation, validation, runtime ownership, and the renderer.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="SubChapterSubHeading" id="05-engine-i-ch009-read-a-game-feature-at-three-nested-scales">Read a game feature at three nested scales&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content">A game system is a set of interacting parts that forms a larger whole. To inspect one, name four things: its <Strong aid:cstyle="Bold">objects</Strong> (the parts), their <Strong aid:cstyle="Bold">attributes</Strong> (properties and state), their <Strong aid:cstyle="Bold">internal relationships</Strong> (how the parts affect one another), and the <Strong aid:cstyle="Bold">environment</Strong> (the context around the system). These labels depend on the question being asked; they are a lens for analysis, not a required software architecture. Salen and Zimmerman’s chess example shows why the lens matters: the same board game can be examined as a formal rule system, as an experience between players, or as a cultural object. The book describes these systems as nested: rules are experienced through play, and play sits in a wider cultural context. (Rules of Play, PDF pp. 63–68.)&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Figure"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/eb6c69e4fb6d1a760a99797aa30f16494e9b21492ebdca1266ed9d9f63074d7d.pdf" alt="Diagram" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/mermaid/f2ae246ff7ac23affcdf5688.svg" sourceWidthPt="426.820312" sourceHeightPt="236.849991" baseFontPt="12.0" />&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Caption">One shared-kit interaction can be examined as formal rules, participant experience, and cultural expectations.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content"><Strong aid:cstyle="Bold">Read the figure:</Strong> start with the same interaction. Each branch asks a different question and calls for different evidence: a state transition, participants’ understanding, or the surrounding practice.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">Test a long sequence diagram at the final page width&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Figure"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/2f2c960121f83174dcb6f046be954d14331520c631f3c6ddca8195de06bef8a0.pdf" alt="Diagram" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/mermaid/12f60b7ab1e672dd10535591.svg" sourceWidthPt="493.5" sourceHeightPt="608.25" baseFontPt="12.0" />&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Caption">A validated candidate pipeline can be published at a safe boundary while old GPU work drains before resource retirement.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">Keep the full message flow readable&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Figure"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/18d97b56d6f678a7836228729d0ce374c6e914ffbb678de0876722e3cabcbca2.pdf" alt="Diagram" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/mermaid/8e675126df1a1b1854a18b23.svg" sourceWidthPt="379.5" sourceHeightPt="609.75" baseFontPt="12.0" />&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Caption">The sequence follows file changes through compilation, pipeline validation, renderer publication, in-flight work, and safe retirement.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">Read a two-panel process as one connected diagram&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Figure"><Image href="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/print/8390e2b914e3b139230278b966faa0f00e254513c1ddf1dc6f2d740dc7de7acf.pdf" alt="Diagram" originalSVG="file:///Users/swayamsingal/Library/Mobile%20Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Master/Book%20Production/AllMight%20Codex/sharedAssets/mermaid/fcbea06ba67e4dcc48784ddf.svg" sourceWidthPt="275.771255" sourceHeightPt="498.150009" baseFontPt="9.75" />&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Caption">The shared command buffer connects asset and batch inputs to scene completion.&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="ProofSectionStart">A table continues as the same comparison&#13;</Content><Content aid:pstyle="Content"><Table aid:table="table" aid:trows="26" aid:tcols="2" sourceHeadRows="1"><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="181.0051031911803"><Content aid:pstyle="Caption">Topic&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="214.9948968088197"><Content aid:pstyle="Caption">Current repository evidence&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwidth="181.0051031911803"><Content aid:pstyle="TableCell">Simple 1D compute&#13;</Content></Cell><Cell aid:table="cell" aid:crows="1" aid:ccols="1" aid:ccolwi